#slide()[
#text(size: 30pt, weight: "bold")[Rationality in Traditional Finance]
#v(40pt)
#only("1-")[- Investors make decisions to maximize their utility 📈]
#v(20pt)
#only("2-")[- Based on all available information 🗞️]
#v(20pt)
#only("3-")[- Utility: Measure of satisfaction or benefit 😊]
#only("1")[
#voiceover("In traditional finance, rationality means that investors make decisions with the goal of maximizing their utility.")
]
#only("2")[
#voiceover("They base these decisions on all the information that is available to them.")
]
#only("3")[
#voiceover("Utility is a measure of the satisfaction or benefit that an investor derives from a particular outcome.")
]
]


#slide()[
#text(size: 30pt, weight: "bold")[Utility Maximization]
#v(40pt)
#only("1-")[- Investors choose the option with the highest expected utility]
#v(20pt)
#only("2-")[- Example: Invest in A (utility: \$10) or B (utility: \$8)?]
#v(20pt)
#only("3-")[- Rational investor chooses A 🅰️]
#only("1")[
#voiceover("According to the principle of utility maximization, investors will always choose the option that they expect to provide them with the highest utility.")
]
#only("2")[
#voiceover("For example, if an investor has the choice between investment A with an expected utility of 10 and investment B with an expected utility of 8, ...")
]
#only("3")[
#voiceover("... a rational investor will choose investment A, as it offers the higher utility.")
]
]


#slide()[
#text(size: 30pt, weight: "bold")[Information Efficiency]
#v(40pt)
#only("1-")[- Rational investors incorporate all available information 🧠]
#v(20pt)
#only("2-")[- Prices reflect all known information 📊]
#v(20pt)
#only("3-")[- No systematic way to "beat the market" 🏆]
#only("1")[
#voiceover("Rational investors are assumed to incorporate all available information into their decision-making process.")
]
#only("2")[
#voiceover("As a result, market prices are thought to reflect all known information.")
]
#only("3")[
#voiceover("This implies that there is no systematic way to \"beat the market\" and achieve returns higher than the market average.")
]
]


#slide()[
#text(size: 30pt, weight: "bold")[Summary]
#v(40pt)
#only("1-")[- Rationality: Investors maximize utility based on all information]
#v(20pt)
#only("2-")[- Utility maximization: Choose option with highest expected utility]
#v(20pt)
#only("3-")[- Information efficiency: Prices reflect all known information]
#only("1")[
#voiceover("In summary, rationality in traditional finance means that investors make decisions to maximize their utility based on all available information.")
]
#only("2")[
#voiceover("They do this by always choosing the option that offers the highest expected utility.")
]
#only("3")[
#voiceover("This leads to information efficiency, where market prices are thought to reflect all known information, making it impossible to systematically outperform the market.")
]
]